#! ia 1.0

@system ia-authoring-host
  provider "local"
  version "0.1.0"
  describes "The host-authoring part of the IA authoring kit: how skills, agents, hooks and plugins become IA-owned artifacts. Four activities (lower, project, evaluate, qualify), each a capability with its playbook, the role briefs that run them, the checks the core's check runner may run, the trigger-evaluation protocol as conventions, and its runner and config reference as kit assets. This system mints no words and grants no authority."
  steward @agent host-authoring-steward
  requires
    - agent-system
    - agent-composition-system
    - workspace-system
    - governance-system
    - compliance-system

@agent host-authoring-steward
  meaning
    says "Owns the records of the IA authoring kit's host-authoring part and reviews every change to them."
    answers "Who owns the host-authoring part of the IA authoring kit?"
  governance
    applies [convention, playbook, contract, check, case, capability, agent]
